# MjengoOS — trivy ignore list (.github/workflows/publish.yml gate).
#
# POLICY (issue #209):
#   · The publish gate fails on HIGH/CRITICAL findings that HAVE a fix
#     available (ignore-unfixed: true — unfixed upstream findings stay
#     visible in the scan table but don't gate, because no action this
#     repo can take would clear them; watch them in the table).
#   · This file is the ONLY place a finding may be permanently silenced.
#     An entry here is a reviewed, time-boxed decision — never a reflex.
#
# ENTRY FORMAT (trivy):
#   <CVE-or-advisory-id>
#
#   ...with a mandatory comment block above every entry:
#     - WHAT: the finding, the package, the image (app/website)
#     - WHY IGNORED: not reachable / accepted risk / vendor-declared
#       non-issue — the reasoning a reviewer needs
#     - EXPIRY: <YYYY-MM-DD> — the date this exemption must be re-triaged
#       (a stale expiry is a review finding in itself; quarterly sweep)
#     - REVIEWER: who accepted it (GitHub handle)
#
# EXAMPLE (commented out — nothing is ignored today; keep it that way):
# CVE-2024-00000
#   WHAT: example-only entry — libfoo 1.2.3 in the app image
#   WHY IGNORED: not reachable — the vulnerable codepath needs a feature
#     this image never executes at runtime
#   EXPIRY: 2027-01-01
#   REVIEWER: @Roy-Wanyoike
#
# CURRENT CONTENT: empty by design. The first real scan decides whether
# the Debian slim base's finding set clears the gate as-is.
